ADVANCED SQL QUERIES

The project includes 16 SQL queries covering all major DBMS features.

Q1 — Simple SELECT

```sql
SELECT Student_ID AS ROLL_NO, Student_Name AS STUDENT_NAME, Email AS EMAIL_ID
FROM STUDENT;
```

Q2 — WHERE with AND

```sql
SELECT Student_ID, Student_Name, Department
FROM STUDENT
WHERE Department = 'CSE' AND Student_ID >= 1019
ORDER BY Student_ID;
```

Q3 — WHERE + ORDER BY DESC

```sql
SELECT Exam_Title, Exam_Date, Exam_Type
FROM EXAM
WHERE Exam_Type = 'FINAL'
ORDER BY Exam_Date DESC;
```

Q4 — Aggregate Functions

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS TOTAL_ATTEMPTS,
       ROUND(AVG(Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVG_MARKS,
       MAX(Marks_Obtained) AS HIGHEST,
       MIN(Marks_Obtained) AS LOWEST,
       SUM(Marks_Obtained) AS TOTAL_MARKS_SCORED
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT;
```

Q5 — GROUP BY

```sql
SELECT Exam_ID, COUNT(*) AS STUDENTS_APPEARED,
       ROUND(AVG(Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVG_MARKS,
       MAX(Marks_Obtained) AS MAX_MARKS,
       MIN(Marks_Obtained) AS MIN_MARKS
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
GROUP BY Exam_ID
ORDER BY Exam_ID;
```

Q6 — GROUP BY + HAVING

```sql
SELECT Exam_ID, COUNT(*) AS STUDENTS_APPEARED,
       ROUND(AVG(Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVG_MARKS
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
GROUP BY Exam_ID
HAVING AVG(Marks_Obtained) > 60
ORDER BY AVG_MARKS DESC;
```

Q7 — HAVING with JOIN

```sql
SELECT c.Course_Name, COUNT(*) AS ENROLLED_STUDENTS
FROM COURSE c
JOIN ENROLLMENT e ON e.Course_ID = c.Course_ID
GROUP BY c.Course_Name
HAVING COUNT(*) >= 4
ORDER BY ENROLLED_STUDENTS DESC;
```

Q8 — INNER JOIN (3 tables)

```sql
SELECT a.Attempt_ID, s.Student_ID, s.Student_Name, x.Exam_Title, a.Marks_Obtained
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT a
JOIN STUDENT s ON s.Student_ID = a.Student_ID
JOIN EXAM x ON x.Exam_ID = a.Exam_ID
ORDER BY x.Exam_ID, a.Marks_Obtained DESC;
```

Q9 — INNER JOIN + GROUP BY + HAVING + CASE

```sql
SELECT c.Course_Name,
       COUNT(a.Attempt_ID) AS STUDENTS_APPEARED,
       SUM(CASE WHEN r.Status = 'PASS' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS PASSED,
       ROUND(AVG(a.Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVG_MARKS
FROM COURSE c
JOIN EXAM x ON x.Course_ID = c.Course_ID
JOIN EXAM_ATTEMPT a ON a.Exam_ID = x.Exam_ID
JOIN RESULT r ON r.Attempt_ID = a.Attempt_ID
GROUP BY c.Course_Name
HAVING AVG(a.Marks_Obtained) >= 60
ORDER BY AVG_MARKS DESC;
```

Q10 — LEFT JOIN

```sql
SELECT s.Student_ID, s.Student_Name, COUNT(e.Course_ID) AS COURSES_ENROLLED
FROM STUDENT s
LEFT JOIN ENROLLMENT e ON e.Student_ID = s.Student_ID
GROUP BY s.Student_ID, s.Student_Name
ORDER BY COURSES_ENROLLED DESC, s.Student_ID;
```

Q11 — Anti-Join using LEFT JOIN

```sql
SELECT s.Student_ID, s.Student_Name
FROM STUDENT s
LEFT JOIN EXAM_ATTEMPT a
       ON a.Student_ID = s.Student_ID AND a.Exam_ID = 201
WHERE a.Attempt_ID IS NULL
ORDER BY s.Student_ID;
```

Q12 — Scalar Subquery

```sql
SELECT Attempt_ID, Student_ID, Exam_ID, Marks_Obtained
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
WHERE Marks_Obtained > (SELECT AVG(Marks_Obtained) FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT)
ORDER BY Marks_Obtained DESC;
```

Q13 — IN Subquery

```sql
SELECT Exam_ID, Exam_Title, Exam_Date
FROM EXAM
WHERE Exam_ID IN (
    SELECT Exam_ID
    FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
    GROUP BY Exam_ID
    HAVING AVG(Marks_Obtained) >= 75
)
ORDER BY Exam_ID;
```

Q14 — Correlated Subquery with NOT EXISTS

```sql
SELECT Student_ID, Student_Name, Department
FROM STUDENT s
WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1
    FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT a
    WHERE a.Student_ID = s.Student_ID
);
```

Q15 — Derived Table

```sql
SELECT T.EXAM_ID, T.STUDENTS, T.AVG_MARKS
FROM (
    SELECT Exam_ID, COUNT(*) AS STUDENTS,
           ROUND(AVG(Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVG_MARKS
    FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
    GROUP BY Exam_ID
) AS T
WHERE T.AVG_MARKS > 60
ORDER BY T.AVG_MARKS DESC;
```

Q16 — MAX() Subquery

```sql
SELECT s.Student_Name, a.Marks_Obtained
FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT a
JOIN STUDENT s ON s.Student_ID = a.Student_ID
WHERE a.Exam_ID = 201
  AND a.Marks_Obtained = (
      SELECT MAX(Marks_Obtained)
      FROM EXAM_ATTEMPT
      WHERE Exam_ID = 201
  );
```

VIEWS

The project includes 3 views.

1. V_STUDENT_REPORT

```sql
CREATE VIEW V_STUDENT_REPORT AS
SELECT s.Student_ID, s.Student_Name, s.Department, c.Course_Name,
       x.Exam_Title, x.Exam_Date, a.Marks_Obtained,
       r.Percentage, r.Grade, r.Status
FROM STUDENT s
JOIN EXAM_ATTEMPT a ON a.Student_ID = s.Student_ID
JOIN EXAM x ON x.Exam_ID = a.Exam_ID
JOIN COURSE c ON c.Course_ID = x.Course_ID
JOIN RESULT r ON r.Attempt_ID = a.Attempt_ID;
```

Purpose: Ready-made mark sheet for front-end use.

2. V_COURSE_ANALYTICS

```sql
CREATE VIEW V_COURSE_ANALYTICS AS
SELECT c.Course_ID, c.Course_Name, i.Instructor_Name,
       COUNT(a.Attempt_ID) AS TOTAL_ATTEMPTS,
       ROUND(AVG(a.Marks_Obtained),2) AS AVERAGE_MARKS,
       SUM(CASE WHEN r.Status = 'PASS' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS PASSED,
       SUM(CASE WHEN r.Status = 'FAIL' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS FAILED
FROM COURSE c
LEFT JOIN EXAM x ON x.Course_ID = c.Course_ID
LEFT JOIN EXAM_ATTEMPT a ON a.Exam_ID = x.Exam_ID
LEFT JOIN RESULT r ON r.Attempt_ID = a.Attempt_ID
LEFT JOIN INSTRUCTOR i ON i.Instructor_ID = c.Instructor_ID
GROUP BY c.Course_ID, c.Course_Name, i.Instructor_Name;
```

Purpose: Faculty dashboard and course-wise performance analysis.

3. V_UPCOMING_EXAMS

```sql
CREATE VIEW V_UPCOMING_EXAMS AS
SELECT x.Exam_ID, x.Exam_Title, c.Course_Name, i.Instructor_Name,
       x.Exam_Date, x.Duration_Minutes, x.Total_Marks, x.Exam_Type
FROM EXAM x
JOIN COURSE c ON c.Course_ID = x.Course_ID
JOIN INSTRUCTOR i ON i.Instructor_ID = c.Instructor_ID
WHERE x.Exam_Date > CURDATE();
```

